DED|OPUS_MEDIA_REFETCH_NEEDED","claim_present":"no","claim_record_errors":"","decision_origin":"opus_checkpoint2","exhausted_steps":"","instrument_id":"EO:12506","provisional_status":"no","ready_for_human_review":"no","ready_tier":"","step_clause_inventory":"open","step_counterevidence":"open","step_ending_or_current_basis":"open","step_opus_media":"open","step_original_text":"open","step_provisional_status":"done","step_savings_residuals":"open","step_shared_sources":"n/a","steps_applicable":"7","steps_done":"1"},"readiness_blockers":[{"step":"original_text","what":"no official original-text candidate from any job"},{"step":"ending_or_current_basis","what":"provisional NO, but no job found a whole-order-end candidate"}],"schema":"eo-case-bundle/v1","status":"no","text_pointers":[{"first_1500_characters":"Executive Order 12506—Nuclear Cooperation With EURATOM\nMarch 04, 1985\nBy the authority vested in me as President by the Constitution and statutes of the United States of America, including Section 126a(2) of the Atomic Energy Act of 1954, as amended (42 U.S.C. 2155(a)(2)), and having determined that, upon the expiration of the period specified in the first proviso to Section 126a(2) of such Act and extended by Executive Orders No. 12193, 12295, 12351, 12409 and 12463, failure to continue peaceful nuclear cooperation with the European Atomic Energy Community would be seriously prejudicial to the achievement of the United States nonproliferation objectives and would otherwise jeopardize the common defense and security of the United States, and having notified the Congress of this determination, I hereby extend the duration of that period to March 10, 1986.\nRONALD REAGAN\nThe White House,\nMarch 4, 1985.","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-opus_zip-12506-e27d3f46b9.txt","sha256":"8b6f20c54ee7b885edea90ff3e1a6936fdaa46b781652757b4bb72103b25e703","source":{"line":864,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"8809e9eb8b346f02b83202f493af46e1a18c47dfb91cce80483d28dfb281ff4d"}},{"first_1500_characters":"{\"member\": \"usc02.xml\", \"note_id\": \"iddcb8117d-3a6e-11f1-a0f3-db3efcbbb4ee\", \"citation\": \"2 U.S.C. 685 note\", \"heading\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845. Delegation of Certain Reporting Functions to Director of Office of Management and Budget\", \"subjects\": [\"11845\"], \"status_line\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845, Mar. 24, 1975, 40 F.R. 13299, as amended by Ex. Ord. No. 12608, Sept. 9, 1987, 52 F.R. 34617, provided:\", \"text\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845. Delegation of Certain Reporting Functions to Director of Office of Management and Budget\\nEx. Ord. No. 11845, Mar. 24, 1975, 40 F.R. 13299, as amended by Ex. Ord. No. 12608, Sept. 9, 1987, 52 F.R. 34617, provided:\\nBy virtue of the authority vested in me by the Impoundment Control Act of 1974 (Public Law 93–344; 88 Stat. 332, (2 U.S.C. 681 et seq.), hereinafter referred to as the Act) [subchapters I and II of this chapter], and section 301 of title 3 of the United States Code, the Director of the Office of Management and Budget is hereby designated and empowered to exercise, as of October 1, 1974 without ratification or other action of the President (1) the functions required by sections 1014(b) and 1014(d) of the Act [subsecs. (b) and (d) of this section] of transmitting to the Comptroller General of the United States and to the Office of the Federal Register copies of special messages transmitted pursuant to section 1012 or 1013 (2 U.S.C. 683 and 684) of the Act; and (2) the function conferred upon the President by section 1014(e) of the Act (2 U.S.C. 685","path":"jobs/current-law/output/USC_EO_NOTES.jsonl","sha256":"ac1e287b6b606b8adc5c1975f662aae2d31989c1d072e32c89dbc38f6efe8016","source":{"line":3,"path":"jobs/current-law/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"5b6e5de61be4ea9c9c4749827c02d0c9d484107505b7e9adae3172a42351c188"}}]}
